  data: {
    LLM: "With 5 cards to choose from, you should rarely play a hand that isn't at least a Flush. Look for high pairs or consecutive suit sequences.\n\nThe 'Hidden' Prial: If you are dealt a pair and two cards of another suit, evaluate if it's better to keep the pair for a safe 'Seeing' bet or gamble on a 'Blind' bet with potentially higher hidden value.\n\nDiscard Tracking: Since every player mucks two cards, 8-16 cards are taken out of play in a 4-8 player game. Track which ranks are most common in your 5 cards to deduce which suits/ranks are depleted in opponents' hands.",
    Player: "With 5 cards to choose from, you should rarely play a hand that isn't at least a Flush. Look for high pairs or consecutive suit sequences.\n\nThe 'Hidden' Prial: If you are dealt a pair and two cards of another suit, evaluate if it's better to keep the pair for a safe 'Seeing' bet or gamble on a 'Blind' bet with potentially higher hidden value.\n\nDiscard Tracking: Since every player mucks two cards, 8-16 cards are taken out of play in a 4-8 player game. Track which ranks are most common in your 5 cards to deduce which suits/ranks are depleted in opponents' hands.",
